<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="2.0">

  <category>
    <pattern>ROYALTIES</pattern>
    <template>Your royalty split is 80/20 — you keep 80% of all royalties generated by your commissioned work. Brass Note Studios retains 20% as a publishing royalty, which is standard for bespoke production houses. We handle all PRO registration on your behalf.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT ARE THE ROYALTIES</pattern>
    <template>Your royalty split is 80/20 — you keep 80% of all royalties generated by your commissioned song. Brass Note Studios retains 20% as a publishing royalty, standard for bespoke production houses. This covers streaming, sync licensing, broadcast, social media, and live performance. We handle PRO registration on your behalf.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT ARE YOUR ROYALTIES</pattern>
    <template>Our royalty model is 80/20 — 80% goes to you, 20% is retained by Brass Note Studios as a publishing royalty. Your 80% covers all commercial uses: streaming, sync, broadcast, social media, and live performance. We register with performing rights organizations on your behalf.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO ROYALTIES WORK</pattern>
    <template>Every commissioned song carries an 80/20 royalty split. You receive 80% of all royalties generated — from streaming, sync licensing, broadcast, and live performance. Brass Note Studios retains 20% as a standard publishing royalty. We handle PRO registration so your royalties are collected automatically from day one.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>TELL ME ABOUT ROYALTIES</pattern>
    <template>Our royalty split is 80% to you, 20% to Brass Note Studios. Upon delivery you receive full commercial rights — streaming, sync, broadcast, social media, and live performance. We handle all performing rights organization (PRO) registration on your behalf.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>ROYALTY</pattern>
    <template>The royalty split is 80/20 — 80% to you, 20% to Brass Note Studios as a publishing royalty. Your share covers all commercial uses. We handle PRO registration so your royalties flow automatically.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS A ROYALTY</pattern>
    <template>A royalty is a payment you receive when your song is streamed, broadcast, performed live, or licensed for use. With a Brass Note Studios commission, you keep 80% of all royalties generated. We handle the registration paperwork so you don't have to.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>* ROYALT *</pattern>
    <template>Our royalty split is 80% to you, 20% to Brass Note Studios — standard for bespoke production houses. You receive full commercial rights: streaming, sync, broadcast, social, and live performance. We handle PRO registration on your behalf.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>ROYALTY SPLIT</pattern>
    <template>The royalty split is 80% to you, 20% to Brass Note Studios. Your 80% covers streaming, sync licensing, broadcast, social media, and live performance. We handle PRO registration so your royalties flow correctly from day one.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHO OWNS THE RIGHTS</pattern>
    <template>You do — with a publishing royalty retained by Brass Note Studios. Upon delivery, you receive full commercial rights to your commissioned song. You keep 80% of all royalties; the studio retains 20% as a standard publishing split.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>DO YOU KEEP ANY ROYALTIES</pattern>
    <template>Yes — Brass Note Studios retains a 20% publishing royalty, which is standard for bespoke production houses. You receive the remaining 80%, plus full commercial rights covering all uses of your song.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT ABOUT COPYRIGHT</pattern>
    <template>Upon delivery, you receive full commercial rights to your commissioned work. Brass Note Studios retains a 20% publishing royalty interest. We handle PRO (performing rights organization) registration on your behalf so your copyright and royalty collection are properly established.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I SELL THE SONG</pattern>
    <template>Yes — your full commercial rights allow streaming, sync licensing, broadcast, social media, live performance, and more. If you intend to sell the master rights entirely, that can be discussed as part of your commission agreement.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I USE THE SONG COMMERCIALLY</pattern>
    <template>Yes. Your commission includes full commercial rights — streaming platforms, sync licensing, broadcast, YouTube, social media, and live performance. Your 80% royalty share applies to all commercial exploitation of the song.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS PRO REGISTRATION</pattern>
    <template>PRO stands for Performing Rights Organization — bodies like ASCAP, BMI, or SESAC that collect royalties when your music is performed or broadcast publicly. We handle registration on your behalf so that your royalties are collected automatically.</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Streaming / platform rights ────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I PUT IT ON SPOTIFY</pattern>
    <template>Your commission includes full commercial rights — Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube Music, and all major streaming platforms are covered. Your 80% royalty share applies to all streaming revenue, and we handle PRO registration so those royalties flow automatically.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I STREAM IT</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I USE THE SONG COMMERCIALLY</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I RELEASE IT</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I USE THE SONG COMMERCIALLY</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I DISTRIBUTE IT</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I USE THE SONG COMMERCIALLY</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I DO WHAT I WANT WITH IT</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I SELL THE SONG</srai></template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Royalty widening ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

